# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# contractions.mcon - English contractions and the full forms they stand for.
#
# Format: `<full form> | <contraction>[ | <contraction2> ...]`. Parse rewrites a
# contraction as its full form, in the player's input and in every template's
# match tokens alike, so "what's your name" and "what is your name" are one
# question; what an NPC says keeps the template's own spelling. Only words whose
# 's can never be a possessive are listed - "John's" stays a possessive.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

what is   | what's
where is  | where's
who is    | who's
how is    | how's
when is   | when's
why is    | why's
that is   | that's
there is  | there's
here is   | here's
it is     | it's
he is     | he's
she is    | she's

i am      | i'm
you are   | you're
we are    | we're
they are  | they're
what are  | what're
who are   | who're
where are | where're

i have    | i've
you have  | you've
we have   | we've
they have | they've

i will    | i'll
you will  | you'll
he will   | he'll
she will  | she'll
we will   | we'll
they will | they'll
what will | what'll
who will  | who'll

i would   | i'd
you would | you'd
he would  | he'd
she would | she'd
we would  | we'd
they would | they'd

is not    | isn't
are not   | aren't
was not   | wasn't
were not  | weren't
do not    | don't
does not  | doesn't
did not   | didn't
have not  | haven't
has not   | hasn't
had not   | hadn't
cannot    | can't
could not | couldn't
will not  | won't
would not | wouldn't
should not | shouldn't
must not  | mustn't
